# Lazy evaluation: TypeAssert record guard fires only on field access
# Closed record type annotation guards each field with its type.
# Field `bad` contains an error expression but is never accessed.
# If the guard fired eagerly (at assertion time), the test would fail.
# If the guard fires lazily (correct), the test passes because `good` is accessed but `bad` is not.
[@[good: Int  bad: Int] [good: 42  bad: [raise "should not fire"]]]
---
%.good
=== out
Int(42)
